; #122, gap G-5, option B: the test run is offline at the operating system's level, every child process
; included, whatever its language or environment. `make test` runs pytest inside this profile on macOS.
; Loopback stays open (the engine tests' servers), and so do unix sockets but the system resolver's:
; a name lookup would leave the machine through it (the W3 review's M5), and `localhost` resolves
; without it. Every other outbound connection is refused with EPERM before a packet leaves.
; A live contract test (RUN_CONTRACT_TESTS=1) runs outside `make test`, as before.
(version 1)
(allow default)
(deny network-outbound)
(allow network-outbound (remote ip "localhost:*"))
(allow network-outbound (remote unix-socket))
(deny network-outbound (remote unix-socket (path-literal "/private/var/run/mDNSResponder")))
; The resolver's mach service, which Network.framework asks instead of the socket, and LaunchServices,
; through which a child could hand a URL to an app outside this sandbox (the W3 Tester's M7). Read from
; the profile; the whole suite passes with both denied.
(deny mach-lookup (global-name "com.apple.dnssd.service"))
(deny mach-lookup (global-name "com.apple.coreservices.launchservicesd"))
